import HodgeLean.Adapters.AbelianHodgeDischargeProofs

/-! # `HodgeDecomposition` and `CupFiltered` for abelian `X`, and the freed milestones (FROZEN SPEC)

The frozen spec for `docs/briefs/cloud-spec-abl1.md`. Do not edit this file. Each theorem is
proved by the matching `_aux` theorem in `AbelianHodgeDischargeProofs.lean`. Spec doc:
`docs/specs/AbelianHodgeDischarge.md`.

Stage hl5 (`CupLeftFiltrationAbelian.lean`) derives `CupFiltered X (cupProductOf X)` and
`HodgeDecomposition X` for abelian `X` in two anonymous `example`s. The ledger records only named
declarations, so neither derivation is a ledger fact, and no milestone can cite it. This spec names
the two derivations and restates, for abelian `X`, the milestones of
`docs/roadmap/after-hl5-freed.md` §3 that they free.

"Abelian" means `[GrpObj X] [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom]` over
`Spec ℂ`, the four instances of every abelian milestone on `main`.

**Claimed.** For every abelian `X`:
* `HodgeDecomposition X` (C4) and `CupFiltered X (cupProductOf X)` (O5), with no other hypothesis;
* with C1, C2 and C4 supplied by `finbetti_finiteBetti`, `spec_bettiDeRhamIso_abelian` and the
  first named theorem, and at `μ = cupProductOf X` also C7 and O5 supplied by
  `torusCohomology_cupProductOf` and the second named theorem:
  * `IsExteriorOfWeightOne` for the package at `cupProductOf X`, and `weilClassOf … ≤ Hdg^k` for
    every Weil-type action `A`, with no hypothesis at all;
  * the transfer, the `g = 1, 2` milestones, the Weil-class connector and the F-1569 reduction for
    every cup product `μ` (resp. family `cup`) with `TorusCohomology`, as implications from their
    remaining original hypotheses, with `F1569StatementFor cup` read as the equivalent
    `F1569StatementForAbelian cup` (the equivalence is stated here);
  * the `g = 3` milestone, the F-1575 case `m = 1`, and the five `AbelianMilestones.lean`
    milestones, at `cupProductOf X`, as implications from their remaining original hypotheses.

Each `RealDefs` milestone and its `harvestBetti_` twin in `LedgerHarvestBetti.lean` differ only in
`hF : FiniteBetti X`. Once `hF` is supplied they state the same proposition, so each pair gets one
restatement here, with an `example` deriving it from the twin.

**Not claimed.** Nothing for non-abelian `X`, so the two dimension-at-most-3 `_of_cupFiltered`
milestones, which quantify over every smooth projective `X`, are not restated. `CupFiltered X μ` is
not claimed for any `μ` other than `cupProductOf X`. No hypothesis other than C1, C2, C4, C7 (at
`cupProductOf X`) and O5 (at `cupProductOf X`) is discharged: C8, C9, O3, O6, Lefschetz (1,1),
F-1569, generation and `hSU` stay explicit binders wherever the original binds them. No new
`@[hodge_hypothesis]` is added. The Hodge decomposition of an abelian variety is classical.
Relation to the goal: HC no distance; AV milestone no distance.
-/

noncomputable section
open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexPoint TopologicalSpace
open HodgeLean.RealDefs HodgeLean.Foundations HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves

namespace HodgeLean.Adapters

/-- **The Hodge decomposition (C4) for abelian `X`.** For every abelian `X` over `ℂ`, in each
degree the pieces `F^p ∩ conj F^q`, `p + q = n`, form an internal direct sum of `H^n_dR(X)`. This
is hl5's anonymous derivation: hlred's `spec_hodgeDecomposition_of_cupLeft_alone` with
`torusCohomology_cupProductOf` and `spec_cupLeft_cupProductOf`.
Source: Birkenhake–Lange, *Complex Abelian Varieties*, 2nd ed., Grundlehren 302, §1.3 and
Lemma 1.3.1; Voisin, *Hodge Theory and Complex Algebraic Geometry I*, Ch. 6 §6.1; stages hlred
and hl5 (`spec_hodgeDecomposition_of_cupLeft_alone`, `spec_cupLeft_cupProductOf`). -/
theorem hodgeDecomposition_of_abelian (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ))
    [GrpObj X] [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] :
    HodgeDecomposition X :=
  hodgeDecomposition_of_abelian_aux X

/-- hl5's derivation has the same statement. -/
example (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [GrpObj X] [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom]
    [IsProjective X.hom] : HodgeDecomposition X :=
  spec_hodgeDecomposition_of_cupLeft_alone X (torusCohomology_cupProductOf X)
    (spec_cupLeft_cupProductOf X)

/-- **`CupFiltered X (cupProductOf X)` (O5) for abelian `X`.** For every abelian `X` over `ℂ`,
the cup product `cupProductOf X` maps `F^p ⊗ F^q` into `F^(p+q)` under the Betti–de Rham map. This
is hl5's anonymous derivation: hlred's `spec_cupFiltered_of_cupLeft_alone` with
`torusCohomology_cupProductOf` and `spec_cupLeft_cupProductOf`.
Source: Voisin, *Hodge Theory and Complex Algebraic Geometry I*, §5.3 and Ch. 7 §7.1;
Birkenhake–Lange, *Complex Abelian Varieties*, 2nd ed., Grundlehren 302, Lemma 1.3.1; stages
hlred and hl5 (`spec_cupFiltered_of_cupLeft_alone`, `spec_cupLeft_cupProductOf`). -/
theorem cupFiltered_cupProductOf_of_abelian (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ))
    [GrpObj X] [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] :
    CupFiltered X (cupProductOf X) :=
  cupFiltered_cupProductOf_of_abelian_aux X

/-- hl5's derivation has the same statement. -/
example (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [GrpObj X] [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom]
    [IsProjective X.hom] : CupFiltered X (cupProductOf X) :=
  spec_cupFiltered_of_cupLeft_alone X (torusCohomology_cupProductOf X)
    (spec_cupLeft_cupProductOf X)

/-- On the cubic `E`, both hold. -/
example : HodgeDecomposition E ∧ CupFiltered E (cupProductOf E) :=
  ⟨hodgeDecomposition_of_abelian E, cupFiltered_cupProductOf_of_abelian E⟩

/-- **F-1569 with C1, C2 and C4 supplied is F-1569.** `F1569StatementForAbelian cup`, the
statement with its inner proofs of `FiniteBetti X`, `BettiDeRhamIso X` and `HodgeDecomposition X`
supplied, is equivalent to `F1569StatementFor cup`. Forward: given any `hF`, `hB`, `hD`, apply the
hypothesis, by proof irrelevance. Backward: instantiate them at the supplied proofs.
Source: F-1569 (register), as for `F1569StatementFor` (`RealDefs/F1569.lean`); C1, C2, C4 through
`finbetti_finiteBetti`, `spec_bettiDeRhamIso_abelian` and `hodgeDecomposition_of_abelian`. -/
theorem f1569StatementForAbelian_iff
    (cup : ∀ (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom]
      [IsProjective X.hom], CupProduct X) :
    F1569StatementForAbelian cup ↔ F1569StatementFor cup :=
  f1569StatementForAbelian_iff_aux cup

/-- With harvest 2's equivalence, it is also equivalent to `F1569StatementForBetti cup`. -/
example (cup : ∀ (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom]
      [IsProjective X.hom], CupProduct X) :
    F1569StatementForAbelian cup ↔ F1569StatementForBetti cup :=
  (f1569StatementForAbelian_iff cup).trans (harvestBetti_f1569StatementForBetti_iff cup).symm

section Restatements

variable (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [GrpObj X] [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom]
